- English Language Proficiency Requirements Nonnative Speaker Testing Requirements If your native language is not English, official results from the Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL) * , the International English Language Testing System (IELTS) or its online equivalent (IELTS Online), the Duolingo English Test (DET), or the Cambridge English Assessment are required.
- Scores should be no more than two years old at the time of application, and we prefer that you submit all English proficiency test results from the past two years.
- * Should a student take the TOEFL more than once, we'll use the set of TOEFL scores corresponding with the highest overall score.
- We don't use TOEFL MyBest scores, which ‘superscore’ subsection results from more than one test administration of the TOEFL.
- Accepted Scores IELTS We require at least a 7.5 overall band score on either the paper-based or computer-delivered Academic Examination and give consideration to those with subscores of 7.5 and above.
- When sending your official IELTS scores, please ensure that you choose “Carnegie Mellon University – Office of Undergraduate Admission" as the recipient for your score report.
- TOEFL iBT or iBT Home Edition For exams taken before Jan.
- Carnegie Mellon's TOEFL Code is 2074 .

